# Architecture Diagram Explanation Rules

---
description: Rules for automatically generating architecture diagrams when explaining systems or features
globs: **/*
alwaysApply: true
---

## Core Principles

- **Visual First**: Always create diagrams before text explanations
- **Hierarchical Structure**: Explain from overview → components → details
- **Interactive Representation**: Clearly distinguish user flows from data flows
- **Practical Approach**: Create diagrams that aid understanding and implementation

## Automatic Trigger Keywords

When users mention these keywords, **automatically activate architecture diagram explanation mode**:

- "구조를 설명해줘" / "explain the structure"
- "어떻게 동작하는지 보여줘" / "show how it works"
- "시스템을 그려줘" / "draw the system"
- "아키텍처를 설명해줘" / "explain the architecture"
- "흐름을 보여줘" / "show the flow"
- "설계를 시각화해줘" / "visualize the design"
- "다이어그램으로 설명해줘" / "explain with diagrams"

## Mandatory Application Scenarios

Always apply when explaining:
- ✅ New features
- ✅ System architecture
- ✅ Data flows
- ✅ User interfaces
- ✅ API design
- ✅ Database structure

## Diagram Types and Usage

### 🔄 Flowcharts
**When to use**: Processes, workflows, decision flows
```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Start] --> B{Condition Check}
    B -->|Yes| C[Process A]
    B -->|No| D[Process B]
    C --> E[Result]
    D --> E
```

**Use cases**:
- User authentication flows
- File upload processes
- Data validation logic
- Error handling flows

### 🏗️ System Diagrams
**When to use**: Overall system structure, component relationships
```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Frontend"
        A[React Components]
        B[State Management]
    end
    subgraph "Backend"
        C[API Server]
        D[Database]
    end
    A --> C
    C --> D
```

**Use cases**:
- Microservice architecture
- Frontend-backend structure
- Database relationships
- External service integration

### 📊 Sequence Diagrams
**When to use**: Time-ordered interactions
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant F as Frontend
    participant B as Backend
    participant D as Database
    
    U->>F: Request
    F->>B: API Call
    B->>D: Data Query
    D-->>B: Result Return
    B-->>F: Response
    F-->>U: Screen Update
```

**Use cases**:
- API call flows
- User interactions
- Data synchronization
- Real-time communication

### 🗂️ Entity Relationship Diagrams
**When to use**: Database structure, data models
```mermaid
erDiagram
    CUSTOMER ||--o{ ORDER : places
    ORDER ||--|{ LINE-ITEM : contains
    PRODUCT ||--o{ LINE-ITEM : includes
```

**Use cases**:
- Database schema
- Table relationships
- Data modeling
- Normalization structure

## Standard Explanation Structure

```markdown
## 🏗️ [Feature Name] Architecture

### 📋 System Components
[Insert Diagram]

#### 1️⃣ [Layer/Area 1]
- **Role**: Main function description
- **Components**: Detailed component list
- **Responsibility**: Assigned roles

#### 2️⃣ [Layer/Area 2]
- **Role**: Main function description
- **Components**: Detailed component list
- **Responsibility**: Assigned roles

### 🔄 Data Flow
[Sequence Diagram or Flowchart]

### 🎨 UI/UX Features
- **Color Coding**: Meaning of each element's color
- **Icon System**: Used icons and their meanings
- **User Feedback**: Interaction elements

### 🔧 Technical Implementation
```typescript
// Core code examples
```

### 📊 Performance Optimization
- **Optimization Point 1**: Specific methods
- **Optimization Point 2**: Specific methods
```

## Pre-Diagram Checklist

1. [ ] Clearly define the scope of the system to explain
2. [ ] Identify start and end points from user perspective
3. [ ] Understand major components and interactions
4. [ ] Confirm data flow directionality
5. [ ] Consider exception cases and error handling

## During Diagram Creation Checklist

1. [ ] Select appropriate diagram type
2. [ ] Apply standard color palette
3. [ ] Use consistent icon system
4. [ ] Provide clear labeling and descriptions
5. [ ] Organize information hierarchically

## During Explanation Checklist

1. [ ] Diagram first, text explanation later
2. [ ] Follow overview → parts → details order
3. [ ] Specify role and responsibility of each component
4. [ ] Explain data flows and interactions
5. [ ] Include technical implementation code examples

## Post-Completion Review Checklist

1. [ ] Verify consistency between diagram and explanation
2. [ ] Review if beginners can understand
3. [ ] Check if information helps actual implementation
4. [ ] Mention performance optimization aspects
5. [ ] Include future extensibility considerations

## Automatic Application Process

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[User Question] --> B{Keyword Detection}
    B -->|Yes| C[Architecture Explanation Mode]
    B -->|No| D[General Explanation Mode]
    
    C --> E[Generate Diagram]
    E --> F[Structured Explanation]
    F --> G[Code Examples]
    G --> H[Optimization Tips]
    
    D --> I[Text-focused Explanation]
```

